<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Layout xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
      NEW layout. The four STOCK Case layouts are re-ignored by exact filename in .forceignore,
      one of them because it fails validation on a missing Case.CaseComment quick action. Do not
      copy their quickActionList into this file, and do not edit them.

      THERE IS NO quickActionList BLOCK HERE, deliberately. That block is what breaks
      Case-Case Layout in this org.

      The sync-owned fields are Readonly for a reason. Balance At Open and Days Past Due At Open
      are immutable evidence of what triggered the Case; Current Balance and Current Days Past
      Due are overwritten nightly, so typing into them is discarded without warning. Escalation
      Level is a one-way ladder maintained by automation.

      Status is Required and carries the Path. See pathAssistants/Delinquency_Path, and note the
      two POST-DEPLOY gates recorded there: the pathAssistantEnabled master switch, and the fact
      that record pages are assigned PER APP.

      A whole block of standard Case fields (ContactId, Origin, the four Supplied* web-to-case fields, AccountId, Type, Comments, the Contact* fields and ClosedDate) is carried here ONLY because the platform requires a Case layout to contain them. A Case layout omitting either is rejected at deploy time with: Layout must contain an item for required layout field <name>. The deploy reports only the FIRST missing one per run, so fixing them one at a time costs one full validation each; the set was taken wholesale from the stock Case-Case Layout instead. They are Readonly except Comments, which the platform refuses to accept as Readonly (Field:Comments must not be Readonly). Nothing populates any of them, and they are grouped in their own section so they do not clutter the delinquency workflow above.
      It is NOT the tenant identity and nothing populates it. There is no Tenant object in this org and no tenant Accounts exist, so tenant identity hangs off Unit__c and the Receivables Summary mirror. Leave it blank.
      THE PAYMENT COMMITMENTS RELATED LIST IS DEPLOYED IN A SECOND PASS, NOT THIS ONE.
      A Layout is validated against the schema ALREADY COMMITTED in the org, not against the
      payload it ships in. Payment_Commitment__c.Case__c is a Master-Detail created by this same
      deploy, so a relatedLists block naming Payment_Commitments__r fails check-only with
      Cannot find related list:Payment_Commitments__r, even though the field is right there
      in the payload. The first deploy is therefore inherently TWO PASS. Once pass 1 commits,
      add this block back immediately above showEmailCheckbox and redeploy the layout alone:

          relatedLists:
            fields NAME
            fields Commitment_Type__c
            fields Promised_Amount__c
            fields Due_Date__c
            fields Status__c
            fields Breached_Date__c
            relatedList Payment_Commitments__r

      Until that second pass runs, Payment Commitments are INVISIBLE on the Case page and the
      FSD 5.9.7 promise-to-pay workflow has no UI. Nothing fails loudly when this is skipped.
    -->
